From 22c6fd0bbc50d0585ab57ae192025bfd1c0d112e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:08:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] S5: link cronly accounts to devicebasedauth.org accounts
 over OIDC

Add SESSION routes GET/DELETE /api/dba/link and POST /api/dba/link/start and
/finish ({ code, state }). The vendored createOidcClient runs authorization
code + PKCE against DBA_ISSUER (default https://devicebasedauth.org) with
client cronly.org and redirect ${APP_ORIGIN}/auth/dba/callback, which serves
the workspace. State, nonce and PKCE verifier are kept in the AccountDO,
single use, 10-minute TTL, at most 10 pending, pruned by maintenance.

A new DbaLinkDO, one per DBA account, is the global DBA account -> cronly
account index: lookups on every DBA request spread across objects and a
claim is atomic, so a DBA account links to at most one cronly account. The
AccountDO's dba-link row is the confirming half used for display and
unlink; a claim nobody confirms (an interrupted link) can be taken over.
Linking is free like sign-in and rate-limited to 10 a minute.

DbaLinkDO is exported from the Worker and bound as DBA_LINKS with migration
v3 in both wrangler configs; DBA_ISSUER is a plain var. OpenAPI regenerated.
A fake issuer (test-utils/dba-issuer.js) signs with the vendored issuer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Kwqh8U8CPCyYKphVe92vcV
